    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`). Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` field: **`SILVER`** when `namesakeCount` is 0 and an email is present, otherwise **`BRONZE`**.\n\nSince `OwnerDto` is generated from the OpenAPI spec and the tier derives purely from already-persisted fields (`namesakeCount` + `email`), I exposed it via the DTO + mapper rather than a new pipeline step, so it's computed identically for both `POST /api/owners` and `GET /api/owners/{id}`:\n\n- **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema (generates the DTO field).\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` expression, matching the existing `displayName`/`initials` style:\n  ```java\n  owner.getNamesakeCount() != null && owner.getNamesakeCount() == 0\n      && owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank() ? \"SILVER\" : \"BRONZE\"\n  ```\n\nBoth new acceptance tests (`coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail`, `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail`) and the full test suite pass.",
